PolicyManagerStartAttemptTest
├── When no setup exists
│   ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoSetup carrying the account and the action.
│   └── It should call no method.
├── When the setup was cleared
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoSetup and call no method.
├── When an attempt is already waiting
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_AttemptAlreadyActive naming the waiting attempt and call no method.
├── When the request names a nonce other than the stored one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce carrying both nonces and call no method.
├── When the request was signed under a retired setup
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce even though the rule is identical.
├── When the attempt id is not the next one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId carrying both ids and call no method.
├── When the attempt id was already used
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId naming the next id.
├── When the window has passed
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RequestExpired carrying both times and call no method.
├── When the window ends in this block
│   └── It should open the attempt.
├── When all five prechecks fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoSetup.
├── When the last four prechecks fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_AttemptAlreadyActive.
├── When the last three prechecks fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongSetupNonce.
├── When the last two prechecks fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId.
├── When the window has passed and the body does not match
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RequestExpired.
├── When the body does not hash to the commitment
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_SetupCommitmentMismatch carrying both commitments and call no method.
├── When the body was committed under another action
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_SetupCommitmentMismatch.
├── When a place repeats the previous one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_PlacesNotStrictlyIncreasing naming that place.
├── When a place is below the previous one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_PlacesNotStrictlyIncreasing before recomputing its credential.
├── When a place is past the end of the rule
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_PlaceOutOfRange carrying the place and the count, and never ask its method.
├── When the proof names another method of the rule
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch and never ask that method about the place.
├── When a proof names a method the rule never names
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch and never call that method.
├── When the proof carries another config
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch and never call the method.
├── When the proof carries another salt
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch and never call the method.
├── When a method reports itself stopped
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodStopped before its verify is called.
├── When the stopped method fills the first place
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodStopped and call no verify.
├── When the credential is wrong at a stopped method's place
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_CredentialMismatch without reading the pause.
├── When the body ignores stops
│   ├── It should open the attempt without reading any pause.
│   └── It should record the choice on the attempt.
├── When one method fills several places
│   ├── It should read each method's pause once and verify each proof once.
│   └── It should open the attempt with a proof beyond what the rule needs.
├── When the pause read reverts
│   └── It should open the attempt.
├── When the pause read reverts with true
│   └── It should open the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns a word other than true
│   └── It should open the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns true and more
│   └── It should open the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns less than a word
│   └── It should open the attempt.
├── When the pause read writes state
│   └── It should read no stop and leave the method's storage untouched.
├── When the pause read returns a huge answer
│   └── It should open the attempt on a gas budget that copying the answer would exhaust.
├── When the method reverts
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected naming the place and the method.
├── When the method reverts with the magic value
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns nothing
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method has no code
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns less than a word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns more than a word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns another word
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method returns the selector with a low byte set
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method is a precompile that echoes
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected.
├── When the method writes state while verifying
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected and leave the method's storage untouched.
├── When the method returns a huge answer
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected on a gas budget that copying the answer would exhaust.
├── When the proof approves another payload
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected though the method approves that payload's seal.
├── When a rejected proof sits in a short set
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_ProofRejected rather than PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied.
├── When a clause misses its threshold
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied naming that clause.
├── When the first clause is not filled
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied naming clause zero.
├── When the request carries no proofs
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied naming clause zero and call no method.
├── When every threshold is zero
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied naming clause zero.
├── When the body has no clauses
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_RuleUnsatisfied naming clause zero.
├── When a complete set is accepted
│   ├── It should write the attempt record.
│   ├── It should move the attempt counter to this id and leave the setup.
│   ├── It should emit AttemptStarted alone.
│   └── It should call methods only through static calls and store no part of the rule.
├── When methods repeat across the places
│   └── It should record each method once in the order the proofs first name it.
├── When the wait is zero
│   └── It should set consumableAfter to the block timestamp.
├── When the wait ends at the last uint48 second
│   └── It should store the largest uint48 as consumableAfter.
├── When the wait carries the end past the uint48 width
│   └── It should revert with the arithmetic overflow panic and change nothing.
├── When the block timestamp is past the uint48 width
│   └── It should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast carrying the width and the timestamp.
├── When the window passes after acceptance
│   └── It should leave the attempt record unchanged.
└── When an earlier attempt ended
    └── It should open the next id and move the counter to it.
